    "notes": "Federal default curve and individual-market state curves transcribed from the CMS PDF and machine-checked against its text. Ages 0-14 share one band; \"64\" covers 64 and older. State curves are stored RELATIVE TO AGE 21 = 1.0 as the contract requires: DC and MA are published on a different base (age-21 factors 0.727 and 1.183) and were divided by those values (4 decimals); AL, MN, MS, OR and UT already have 21 = 1.000. AL, MS and OR differ from the federal curve only for ages 0-20, MN only for ages 0-20. New Jersey's state curve applies to the small-group market only and is omitted. NY and VT prohibit age rating (1:1). Tobacco ratios are individual-market values from the CMS state rating table (Connecticut is 1.5:1 in the individual market). sha256 is of the raw source document as downloaded.",
